   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the displaying of\na bus driver's credentials while he or she is on duty and the review of his or\nher files",
    "basePrintNo": "S1817",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1817-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §509-dd, amd §509-m, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1817\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the display-\ning of a bus driver's credentials while he or she is on duty and the\nreview of his or her files\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo require the Department of Motor Vehicles to issue a new credential\nfor individuals qualified to drive a bus under Article 19A of the Vehi-\ncle and Traffic Law and to require the display of valid credentials\nwhile the bus driver is on duty. This will allow passengers to verify\nthat their bus driver has met the requirements to drive the bus and that\nthe bus is inspected and has operating authority.\n\nIt also requires that the Department of Motor Vehicles performs an annu-\nal audit of motor carriers subject to VTL Article 19A requirements at\nleast once a year to ensure that motor carriers are in compliance with\nthe law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends subdivision 1 of section 509-m of the vehicle and\ntraffic law, as amended by chapter 12 of the laws of 2020 by adding by\nadding a new section 509-dd, to require bus driver credentials,\ninspection status, and DOT operating authority to always be displayed\nprominently in the front of the bus while the bus driver is on duty.\nThese must be displayed prominently for passengers and consumers to see\nwhile board-ing, and must be displayed where motor carriers perform\ncontract or common carrier services.\n\nSection 2. Amends subdivision 1 of section 509-m of the vehicle and\ntraffic law, as amended by chapter 12 of the laws of 2020 by adding a\nnew subdivision 8, requiring a motor carrier's records to be reviewed\nannually by the Department of Motor Vehicles, instead of every three\nyears. The new subdivision 8 added to section 509(m) of the Vehicle and\nTraffic Law will require the DMV to issue a new credential annually for\nbus drivers qualified to drive a bus under Article 19A, and such creden-\ntial should be designed to be publically displayed.\n\nSection 3. Sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPrivate charter buses have dramatically increased service within New\nYork State. Consumers are routinely boarding such buses to visit casinos\nand other destinations in and out of New York State. There has been an\nincrease in the number of accidents involving such buses, and some of\nthese accidents have involved drivers who were not qualified and/or\nproperly licensed to drive passenger buses. The public display of a\ncredential issued by the DMV would allow consumers to know if their bus\ndriver is properly licensed and qualified. The public display of said\ncredential is similar to the requirements some municipalities have for\nlivery drivers and for-hire taxis to display a similar credential, or\nfor public bus operators who wear a uniform and identifying information.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-2018: A.8726/S.6921 - Referred to Transportation.\n\n2019-2020: A.2188-B/S.3450-B - Referred to Transportation.\n\n2021-2022: A.3461/S.4450 - Referred to Transportation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on April 1 after being signed into law.\n",
